WEBVTT

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.916
AG: You know you've reached
shared understanding

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:34.187
when a colleague does something
that would be puzzling to most people

00:11:34.211 --> 00:11:35.454
but you get it right away.

00:11:35.478 --> 00:11:37.293
The project manager who cc's the boss

00:11:37.317 --> 00:11:39.198
isn't trying to make everyone look bad.

00:11:39.222 --> 00:11:41.976
She's anxious about your
team's work being overlooked.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.374
The guy in accounts payable

00:11:43.398 --> 00:11:46.034
isn't signing off at 3pm
because he's a slacker.

00:11:46.058 --> 00:11:48.576
He's taking care of his mom, who's ill.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.146
MH: Because if you don't
understand people's contexts,

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:54.576
you can make attributions --
and they're often negative attributions --

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.286
about what other people are doing

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.150
or whether they're working hard enough

00:11:58.174 --> 00:11:59.628
or whether they're distracted

00:11:59.652 --> 00:12:01.196
that are not really fair, right?